      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "you mention that it was half a hear ago, and exactly 6 months ago in october vrchat released ui 2.0 and never had any noted stability updates since then.  that ui was the catalyst of the performance deterioration.  the second biggest drop was the addition of the friends joining notifications with no option to disable, those messages caused huge lag spikes like usual when ppl join but now it would be more likely to crash you as well.  and now with april 13ths 2023.2.1 update many of us are not able to get into other worlds at all.  also a lot of these people with the worst performance after april 13th claim to either be in the midwest or texas.  \n\nim not expecting them to bring stability back to what it was 6months ago but this recent update is most important to focus on a fix because its making the game unplayable for many, and since the exact date lines up directly with 2023.2.1 then reverse engineering should allow them to know exactly where to look (at only the recent additions)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
